# --- omarchy-pi (aarch64) ---
# Removed for the Raspberry Pi port. Everything above installs on aarch64;
# these do not, and none of them are load-bearing for the desktop:
#
#   asdcontrol               Apple Studio Display brightness over USB (x86-only, no Pi use case)
#   qemu-user-static-binfmt  x86 cross-architecture emulation (pointless on an ARM host)
#   dotnet-runtime           no aarch64 package in Arch Linux ARM
#   pinta                    needs dotnet-runtime
#   obs-studio               no aarch64 package; build from the AUR if wanted
#   obsidian                 proprietary Electron app, no aarch64 build published
#
# `nvim` is kept: Arch Linux ARM's `neovim` provides it.
